    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "As shown in Table 20.6, all seven of these composite parameters are defined by gene frequencies and gene effects. Functions of these quantities can yield considerable insight into the mechanistic basis of genetic variation. For example, the quantity $ 2(2H_1 + H_4)/D $ is equal to $ \\sum p_l q_l a_l^2 k_l^2 / \\sum p_l q_l a_l^2 $. Thus,",
